# Retired tasks' logs, moved out of the *.log glob so they stop showing up in
# `ls logs/`. Same personal data as the live logs, so ignore the whole dir —
# logs/*.log above does NOT match a subdirectory. (Currently empty: its contents
# were rolled into the tarball below on 2026-08-05. The rule stays so a future
# archive/ can't be committed by the accident of the directory not existing yet.)
logs/archive/
# Compressed cold storage of pre-2026-07-15 backups (the retired weekly_learnings
# task's only run history, plus four .bak files denser than their live logs).
# Same personal data as everything else in logs/, but NEITHER of the two globs
# above matches a .tar.gz — it landed untracked, 612KB, one `git add .` from
# being committed.
logs/*.tar.gz
# Periodic codebase-audit plans. Kept on disk (each audit reads the previous
# one's "verified clean" section to skip re-deriving it) but deliberately not
# committed: they're a working scratchpad about the repo, not part of it, and a
# finding worth keeping belongs in the code or in the doc it's about.
docs/reviews/
# Raw model bake-off runs (evals/). The harness is committed because a model
# swap recurs; its output is not. Each file is hours of Ollama time against
# whichever models happened to be on this machine, and the numbers go stale the
# moment a model or a prompt changes — a stale committed table would be read as
# current. The conclusion of a run belongs in docs/model-eval.md.
evals/results/
.DS_Store
.claude/
scratchpad
